window.DOCS=[{"u": "index.html", "t": "Welcome", "g": "Start here", "x": "Lumivane is a Shopify theme for beauty and skincare shops. This guide takes you from an empty store to a finished shop, one small step at a time. You do not need to know how to code.  Pick where you are 1 I'm new to Shopify Learn the few words used in this guide, then install the theme. 2 Set up my shop fast A 10-step checklist that gets a good-looking store online. 3 Add colour swatches Show shades and colours as round buttons, step by step. 4 Something looks wrong Find your problem and the fix in plain words. The three presets A preset is a ready-made look. You can switch between them in two clicks and your products and text stay the same. Lumivane Warm, soft and light. Round pill buttons. Good for skincare and everyday beauty. Nightbloom Dark and rich with gold touches and square buttons. Good for luxury and fragrance. Fernmist Sage greens and soft shapes. Good for botanical and wellness brands. What you get A home page built from sections : hero slider, product tabs, ingredient circle, routine steps, shade finder, before and after slider, reviews, blog and more. Colour swatches on product pages and product cards. Quick buy on product cards and a cart drawer that slides in. Filtering, sorting and page numbers on collection pages. Instant search that shows results while you type. Animations that you can turn off. They also switch off for visitors who ask their device for less motion. How to use this guide Each page starts with what you will do, then numbered steps, then tips. Words in bold are things you click or type. Words like section and preset are explained in Before you start . "}, {"u": "before-you-start.html", "t": "Before you start", "g": "Start here", "x": "Five minutes of reading now saves hours later. These are the only words and ideas you need.  What you need A Shopify store on any paid plan, or a development store for testing. A few product photos. Image sizes tells you what works best. A computer. The theme editor works on phones, but a computer is much easier. Words used in this guide Word What it means Theme The design of your whole store. You are installing one called Lumivane. Theme editor The Shopify screen where you change the design. Open it from Online Store \u2192 Themes \u2192 Customize . Preset A ready-made look of the theme: Lumivane, Nightbloom or Fernmist. Template The layout of one kind of page: home, product, collection, blog post and so on. Section A horizontal band on a page, such as a hero image or a list of reviews. You can add, remove and drag sections up and down. Block A small item inside a section, such as one slide or one question in an FAQ. Collection A group of products, such as Skincare or Sale . Variant One version of a product, such as a shade or a size. Option A choice shoppers make, such as Shade or Size . Each option has several values , such as Honey or 30 ml . Swatch A small coloured circle that stands for a colour or shade. Metafield Extra information you can attach to a product. You will rarely need this. How the theme editor works Open it. In Shopify choose Online Store \u2192 Themes , then press Customize next to your theme. Pick a page at the top. The dropdown in the middle of the top bar switches between Home, Products, Collections, Blog and more. Use the left column. It lists the sections of the page. Click one to see its settings. Drag the dots on the left of a section to move it. Use the paintbrush icon for the whole store. This is Theme settings : colours, fonts, buttons, swatches and car"}, {"u": "install.html", "t": "Install the theme", "g": "Start here", "x": "Get Lumivane into your store and choose a look. This takes about five minutes.  Upload the theme In your Shopify admin, open Online Store \u2192 Themes . Scroll to Theme library and press Add theme \u2192 Upload zip file . Choose the lumivane.zip file you downloaded. Do not unzip it. Wait until the upload finishes. The theme appears in the theme library. Press Customize on the new theme to open the editor. Upload the zip, not the folder Shopify only accepts a single .zip file. If you see an error about missing files, check that you did not zip a folder that contains the theme folder. The zip should open straight to the folders assets , config , layout and so on. Choose a preset In the editor, click the paintbrush icon on the left. This is Theme settings . Click Change theme style at the top. Pick Lumivane , Nightbloom or Fernmist . Press Save . What changes when you switch presets Colours, button shapes and the page-change animation change. Your products, pages and text stay exactly as they are. Preview before you publish Press the three dots next to Customize in the theme library and choose Preview . Click around: the home page, a collection, a product, the cart. When you are happy, press Publish . Next step Follow the 10-step quick start . "}, {"u": "quick-start.html", "t": "10-step quick start", "g": "Start here", "x": "The shortest path from a new theme to a shop you are proud of. Do these in order.  Add your logo. In the editor open Header (the top section) and upload your logo. Add a second light logo if the header sits over a dark image. See Header and menu . Add products. In Shopify go to Products \u2192 Add product . Use 3 to 5 photos, a clear title and a short description. See Add products . Add colours or shades. If a product comes in colours or shades, add an option called Color or Shade and follow Colour swatches . Make collections. Go to Products \u2192 Collections and create groups such as Skincare, Makeup and Sale. See Collections . Build the menu. Go to Content \u2192 Menus and edit Main menu . Then select it in the Header. See Header and menu . Set up the home page. Open the Home page in the editor and replace the sample images and text, section by section. See Home page . Create your pages. Add About, Contact and FAQ in Online Store \u2192 Pages . See Pages . Set the cart. In Theme settings open Cart and choose what happens after \"Add to cart\". See Cart . Check on a phone. Use the phone icon at the top of the editor, or open your store on your phone. Publish. In the theme library press Publish . Do not leave sample content The theme ships with sample headlines and images. Replace all of it before you publish. Shoppers notice, and Shopify's Theme Store requires real text on live demo stores. "}, {"u": "image-sizes.html", "t": "Image sizes", "g": "Set up", "x": "Good images make the biggest difference to how your shop looks. Use this page as a cheat sheet.  The simple rules Save photos as JPG or WebP . Use PNG only for cut-outs that need a transparent background. Keep each file under 500 KB . Use a free tool such as squoosh.app to shrink it. Upload images bigger than the size below , never smaller. Shopify makes smaller copies for phones for you. Keep the important part of the photo in the middle . Edges are cropped on phones. Sizes by place Where Size in pixels Shape Product photos 1600 \u00d7 2000 Portrait Home hero, background 2400 \u00d7 1350 Wide Home hero, phone background 900 \u00d7 1200 Tall Home hero, product cut-out 1200 \u00d7 1600 PNG or WebP Portrait, transparent Home hero, small round picture 400 \u00d7 400 Square Cinematic banner 2400 \u00d7 1200 Wide Cinematic banner, phone 900 \u00d7 1400 Tall Collection banner 2400 \u00d7 800 Very wide Category chips 400 \u00d7 400 Square Ingredient circle 800 \u00d7 800 Square Ritual steps, stacking cards, story rows 1200 \u00d7 1200 Square Collection list 1000 \u00d7 1250 Portrait Before and after 1600 \u00d7 1000 each, same framing Wide Shoppable image 2000 \u00d7 1400 Wide Blog post picture 1600 \u00d7 1000 Wide Logo 600 px wide, PNG or SVG Any Favicon 32 \u00d7 32 Square Alt text Alt text is a short description of the image for people who use screen readers. In the editor, click any image and press Edit alt text . Describe what is in the picture, for example \"Frosted glass serum bottle on a pink background\" . Do not start with \"image of\". "}, {"u": "products.html", "t": "Add products", "g": "Set up", "x": "Products are the heart of your shop. Here is how to add one that looks good in this theme.  Add a product In Shopify choose Products \u2192 Add product . Type a title , for example Barrier Serum . Write a description : what it does, who it is for, how to use it, key ingredients. Drag in 3 to 5 photos . The first photo is the one shown on product cards. The second is shown when someone hovers over the card. Set the price . To show a sale, type the old price in Compare-at price . The theme shows the badge for you. Under Variants , press Add options like size or color if the product comes in more than one version. See below. Add the product to a collection on the right side, then press Save . Photo order that works A clean photo of the product on a plain background. The product in a scene (lifestyle photo). The texture of the product. The product being used. The size next to a hand (optional). Options and variants If a product comes in different shades or sizes: Press Add options like size or color . Type the option name . Use Shade or Color for colours. Use Size for sizes. Type each value : Porcelain, Petal, Honey or 30 ml, 50 ml . Set a price and stock for each variant and, if you like, attach a photo to each one. Want round colour swatches? Name the option Color , Colour , Shade or Tone and follow Colour swatches . Any other name, such as Size , shows as text buttons. Sold-out products Set stock to 0 and the theme marks the product as sold out. On the product page a sold-out swatch or size is crossed out so shoppers see it is not available. "}, {"u": "swatches.html", "t": "Colour swatches and shades", "g": "Set up", "x": "Swatches turn a list of shade names into small coloured circles. This page explains how they work and how to set them up, even if you have never done it before.  What shoppers see On a product page , an option such as Shade shows as round colour buttons with the chosen name written next to the title (for example Shade: Honey ). The chosen swatch has a ring and a tick. Hover over a swatch to see its name. A sold-out swatch is faded and crossed out. On a product card , up to four small dots appear under the title, then a number such as +2 for the rest. The 3 ways to give a swatch its colour The theme looks for a colour in this order and uses the first one it finds. Order Method Best when 1 Shopify's own swatch colour on the option value You use Shopify's product category with a Color option. This is the recommended way. 2 Swatch colors list in Theme settings Your shades are custom names such as Honey or Cocoa . 3 A plain colour word such as Black, Red, Navy Your values are simple colour names. Nothing to set up. If a value has no colour from any of the three methods, the whole option shows as text buttons instead. This is on purpose, so you never see a blank circle. Method 1: Shopify's swatch colour Open the product in Shopify and set its Category . Shopify only offers swatch colours for categories that have a Color attribute. Under Variants add the option and choose Color from the list that Shopify offers. Pick each colour from Shopify's list. Shopify stores a swatch colour for each one. Save. The theme picks the colours up automatically. Note Not every beauty category offers the Color attribute, and the colour names Shopify offers may not match your shade names. If that happens, use Method 2. It always works. Method 2: type your own colours (most common for makeup) In t"}, {"u": "header-menu.html", "t": "Header and menu", "g": "Set up", "x": "The header is the bar at the top of every page. It holds your logo, menu, search and cart.  Add your logo In the theme editor open any page and click Header in the left column. Next to Logo press Select and upload your logo. A PNG or SVG that is about 600 px wide works well. If the header sits on top of a dark image, also upload Logo for transparent header (usually a white version). Use Logo width and Logo width on mobile to make it bigger or smaller. Make the menu In Shopify go to Content \u2192 Menus and open Main menu . Press Add menu item . Type a name and choose where it links, for example a collection. To make a dropdown, drag an item slightly to the right under another item. That makes it a child. To make a wide mega menu, add one more level: children that have their own children. Press Save menu . Back in the editor, make sure Menu in the Header says Main menu . Header settings in plain words Setting What it does Desktop layout Choose where the logo and menu sit: logo in the middle, logo on the left, or logo above the menu. Sticky header Always keeps it visible while scrolling. Hide on scroll down shows it again when the shopper scrolls up. Off lets it scroll away. Float over the first section The header sits on top of the first image instead of above it. Pair it with a light logo. Text and icons over media Light or dark text for a floating header. Pick the one that is easy to read on your image. Show country/region selector Needs Shopify Markets. Lets shoppers change country and currency. Show language selector Shows when your store has more than one language. Popular products collection The products shown when a shopper opens search and has not typed anything yet. The announcement bar The thin bar above the header. Open Announcement bar in the editor, then add or e"}, {"u": "collections.html", "t": "Collections, filters and pagination", "g": "Set up", "x": "A collection page lists your products. Here is how to organise them and let shoppers filter and browse.  Create a collection In Shopify choose Products \u2192 Collections \u2192 Create collection . Give it a title such as Skincare and an image. The image appears on the collection list page and in the home page sections. Choose Manual to pick products yourself, or Automated to add products by a rule, for example \"tag is skincare\". Save. Change how a collection page looks In the theme editor choose Collections \u2192 Default collection from the page dropdown. Click Product grid in the left column. Setting What it does Products per page How many products appear before the page buttons. 12 or 16 is a good start. Columns on desktop How many products sit in each row on a computer. Columns on mobile 1 or 2 per row on a phone. Enable filtering Shows filters such as price and availability. Filter layout on desktop Sidebar keeps filters beside the products. Drawer hides them behind a Filter button. Enable sorting Adds the \"Sort by\" menu. Pagination Page numbers , Load more button or Infinite scroll . Page numbers are best for search engines. Turn on filters Filters are set up in Shopify, not in the theme. Install Shopify's free Search &amp; Discovery app from the Shopify App Store. Open the app and choose Filters . Add the filters you want, such as Availability, Price, Product type, or a colour filter. Save. The filters appear on collection pages and on the search page. Colour filters show as swatches If you add a colour filter that uses Shopify's swatch colours, the theme shows the colours as small circles in the filter list. Collection templates A template decides the layout. This theme has two for collections: collection is the standard layout with a banner, category chips, product grid and "}, {"u": "home-page.html", "t": "Build your home page", "g": "Pages", "x": "The home page is made of sections. This page shows how to change them and which ones to keep.  How to edit a section In the editor choose Home page from the page dropdown. Click a section name in the left column. Its settings open. Click a block (for example a slide) to edit its text and image. Drag the dots to reorder, or use the eye icon to hide a section without deleting it. To add a section press Add section and choose from the list. The sections on the home page, top to bottom Section What it is What you change Hero: glow slider The big first screen with up to several slides, a product picture and floating details Headline, text, button, 4 images per slide Scrolling marquee A moving line of short claims The words, for example \"Vegan \u00b7 Cruelty free\" Category chips Round pictures that link to concerns or categories Picture and link for each chip Featured collection Product tabs such as Skincare, Makeup, Body The collection behind each tab Manifesto A big statement with two photos The statement and photos Ingredient orbit Ingredient pictures circling a product One picture and short text per ingredient Ritual steps (pinned) A step-by-step routine Title, text and picture for each step, and the products Featured product One product with its options and buy button Choose the product Shade finder A helper that matches a shade The shades, colours and linked products Cinematic banner A full-screen image that grows as you scroll Image, phone image, headline, button Stacking cards Cards that stack as you scroll Three or more cards with image and text Before and after A slider that compares two pictures Both pictures and the result statistics Story rows Alternating picture and text rows Pictures and text Collection list A list of concerns, each linking to a collection The colle"}, {"u": "product-page.html", "t": "The product page", "g": "Pages", "x": "Where shoppers decide to buy. Here is what each part does and how to tune it.  What is on the page Gallery on the left: swipe or use arrows. The small pictures below jump to a photo. Click a photo to zoom. Title, price and rating on the right, then the variant picker (swatches or buttons), quantity and the Add to cart button. Extra blocks such as benefits, a shade guide and an \"ask an expert\" box. Sections underneath: product story, before and after, reviews and related products. Settings in plain words Open Products \u2192 Default product in the editor and click Product in the left column. Setting What it does Desktop gallery Editorial grid shows photos in a grid. Slider with thumbnails shows one large photo and small pictures underneath or at the side. Image fit Fill crops the photo to fill the frame. Fit shows the whole photo. Show the selected variant image first When a shopper picks a shade, show that shade's photo first. Show sticky add-to-cart bar A small bar that stays at the bottom while scrolling, so the buy button is always near. Photo shape Portrait (4:5), Square , Landscape , or Match the photo to use each photo's own shape. Media width How wide the gallery is compared with the text. Show breadcrumbs A small trail like Home \u203a Skincare \u203a Barrier Serum. Variant picker Click the Variant picker block. Style can be Buttons , Dropdown or Variant images . Colour and shade options show as swatches when every value has a colour. See Colour swatches . Bundles and sets The template product.ritual-set is made for a set of products. In Shopify open the product and choose it under Theme template . \"Complete the routine\" bundle without picking products In the Bundle block you can choose up to three products. If you leave them empty, the theme shows Shopify's own complementary "}, {"u": "cart.html", "t": "Cart and checkout", "g": "Pages", "x": "What happens when someone presses Add to cart, and how to encourage bigger orders.  Open Theme settings (paintbrush) \u2192 Cart . Setting What it does After adding to cart Open cart drawer slides the cart in from the side. Go to cart page takes the shopper to the full cart. Enable order note Lets shoppers write a note for you, for example for a gift. Free shipping goal Type an amount such as 75. A progress bar tells shoppers how close they are. Leave it empty to hide the bar. Show recommendations in cart drawer Suggests products the shopper may add. Cart drawer tone The colour scheme of the drawer. Show discount code field Shows the box where shoppers type a code. Show trust message A short reassuring line near the checkout button. Note Checkout is controlled by Shopify, not the theme. Change checkout colours and logo in Settings \u2192 Checkout and customer accounts \u2192 Customize . Quick buy on product cards When Enable quick buy is on (Theme settings \u2192 Product tiles), each product card shows a button. It opens a small window where shoppers choose a shade or size and add to cart without leaving the page. "}, {"u": "search.html", "t": "Search", "g": "Pages", "x": "The theme shows search results while shoppers type.  Open Theme settings \u2192 Search . Setting What it does Enable search suggestions Shows matching products as the shopper types. Trending searches Words shown as buttons before the shopper types, separated by commas. Example: Serum, SPF, Lip oil. Show vendor Shows the brand name in results. Show price Shows the price in results. Make search better Use clear product titles and add product types and tags. Install Shopify's free Search &amp; Discovery app to add synonyms, such as \"moisturiser\" and \"moisturizer\", and to set up filters. Open Search page in the editor to change how many results show per page. "}, {"u": "blog.html", "t": "Blog and articles", "g": "Pages", "x": "A blog builds trust and brings visitors from search engines.  Write your first article In Shopify go to Content \u2192 Blog posts \u2192 Add blog post . Type a title and write the article. Add a picture of 1600 \u00d7 1000 pixels as the featured image. Choose the blog (the theme's journal uses a blog called Journal , or the one you pick). Press Save . Show posts on the home page Open the home page in the editor and add the Blog posts section. Choose the blog and how many articles to show. Ideas for articles How to build an evening routine, what an ingredient does, how to choose your shade, how to read an ingredient list, and answers to the questions customers ask most. "}, {"u": "pages.html", "t": "Pages (About, Contact, FAQ)", "g": "Pages", "x": "Pages hold content that does not change often. The theme has four ready-made page layouts.  Create a page In Shopify choose Online Store \u2192 Pages \u2192 Add page . Type a title, for example About us . On the right, under Theme template , choose the layout from the table below. Press Save , then open the page in the theme editor to change its sections. Template Use it for page Plain text pages such as Shipping or Terms page.about Your story: banner, statement, rows, numbers, values and founder page.contact Contact details and a form, with a short FAQ page.faq Questions and answers grouped by topic page.ingredients An ingredients page with the orbit and story rows Add the pages to your menu Add each page to the Main menu or Footer menu in Content \u2192 Menus so visitors can find it. "}, {"u": "look-and-feel.html", "t": "Colours, fonts and style", "g": "Customize", "x": "Change the whole look of your store from one place. Everything here is under the paintbrush icon (Theme settings).  Colours Open Color tones . There are six colour schemes . A scheme is a set of matching colours for a background, text and buttons. Each section has a Tone (or Color scheme ) setting where you choose one of the six. Edit a scheme once and every section that uses it changes. Use the first scheme for most sections, a darker one for contrast, and the accent scheme sparingly. Check contrast Text must be easy to read. Light grey text on a light background is hard for many people. Typography Setting What it does Font (display) The font for headings Size scale Makes all heading or body text bigger or smaller in one move. 100 is the normal size. Letter spacing Space between letters in headings. Small negative numbers look elegant. Case Show headings in normal case or all capitals Color italic heading words with the accent In the editor, select a word in a heading and press italic. It then takes the accent colour. Small labels and eyebrows Spaced capitals or Sentence case for the tiny text above headings Layout Setting What it does Page width The widest the content can be on large screens Side padding (desktop) Space on the left and right of the page Space between sections Extra space between sections. Increase it for a more airy page. Grid spacing Space between products in a grid Media corner radius How round the corners of pictures are. 0 is square. Buttons and fields Setting What it does Button shape Pill (fully round), Soft (slightly round) or Square Button hover The effect when a mouse is over a button: Liquid fill, Lift or Text roll Field corner radius Roundness of text boxes Product cards Open Product tiles . Setting What it does Image ratio The shape of the"}, {"u": "motion.html", "t": "Animations and speed", "g": "Customize", "x": "Motion makes the theme feel alive, but fast loading matters more. Here is how to control both.  Animation settings Open Theme settings \u2192 Motion . Setting What it does Enable scroll animations The master switch. Turn it off for a completely still store. Animation energy Calm, Balanced or Expressive. Calm is gentle and quick. Expressive is bolder. Image entrance How pictures appear: Curtain wipe, Soft zoom or Fade Animate headings line by line Headings appear one line at a time Magnetic buttons Buttons lean slightly towards the mouse on computers Custom cursor halo A soft circle that follows the mouse on computers Scroll progress line A thin line at the top that shows how far down the page you are Page transitions The effect when changing pages: None, Soft fade or Curtain rise Reduced motion Visitors who set \"Reduce motion\" on their phone or computer never see scroll animation, whatever you choose here. Keep the store fast Resize and compress every image before uploading. See Image sizes . Use fewer sections on the home page. Each one adds weight. Avoid too many apps. Each app can slow the store. Use a short video (under 10 MB) only if it adds real value. Test with Google PageSpeed Insights and fix the largest images first. "}, {"u": "translations.html", "t": "Text and languages", "g": "Customize", "x": "Change any word the theme shows, or add more languages.  Change a word In the theme library press the three dots next to your theme, then Edit default theme content . Type a word, such as cart , in the search box. Change the text and press Save . Add a language In Shopify go to Settings \u2192 Languages \u2192 Add language . Install Shopify's free Translate &amp; Adapt app and translate your products, pages and theme text there. In the theme editor turn on Show language selector in the Header. "}, {"u": "sections.html", "t": "Sections A to Z", "g": "Reference", "x": "Every section you can add in the theme editor. Use this page to look up what a section does and what you can change in it.  How to add a section In the theme editor press Add section on any page and choose from the list. Sections marked header , footer and announcement live in the page header and footer areas. Header The top of every page: logo, menu, search and cart. You can change: Tone, Mobile menu tone, Logo, Logo for transparent header, Logo width, Logo width on mobile, Menu, Desktop layout, Sticky header, Float over the first section, Text and icons over media, Show country/region selector, Show language selector, Popular products collection. Blocks you can add: Mega menu spotlight. Announcement bar Thin bar above the header with rotating short messages. You can change: Tone, Rotate every, Show social icons on desktop, Show country/language on desktop. Blocks you can add: Message. Footer The bottom of every page: links, newsletter and brand text. You can change: Tone, Top padding, Show giant wordmark, Wordmark text, Show payment icons, Show policy links, Show country/region selector, Show language selector. Blocks you can add: Brand, Menu, Text, Email signup. Hero: glow slider Big first-screen slider with a product picture, a small round picture and a glow background. You can change: Accessible name, Height, Text position, Text color, Auto-rotate slides, Change slides every, Pointer parallax on desktop, Scroll hint. Blocks you can add: Slide. Scrolling marquee A moving line of short claims or pictures. You can change: Tone, Style, Loop duration, Direction, Speed up with scroll, Tilt, Separator, Top padding, Bottom padding. Blocks you can add: Text, Image. Category chips Round pictures that link to categories or concerns. You can change: Tone, Label, Show product c"}, {"u": "troubleshooting.html", "t": "Troubleshooting and FAQ", "g": "Help", "x": "Find the problem you see, then try the fix.  My store looks empty or shows grey shapes The theme ships with sample content, and photos do not transfer when you install. Open each section in the editor and add your own images and text. See Build your home page . Shades or colours show as text, not circles At least one value has no colour. Add every value to Theme settings \u2192 Swatches \u2192 Swatch colors . Full steps are in Colour swatches . The cart drawer does not open Open Theme settings \u2192 Cart and check that After adding to cart is set to Open cart drawer . If you installed a cart app, switch it off to test. Filters do not show on my collection Filters come from Shopify's free Search &amp; Discovery app. Add filters there, then check Enable filtering in the collection's Product grid section. Product cards have no colour dots Turn on Theme settings \u2192 Product tiles \u2192 Show color swatches . The product also needs an option named Color, Shade, Tone or Colour, and every value needs a colour. A section is missing on a page Click the eye icon next to the section in the editor. It may be hidden. Also check that you are editing the right page in the dropdown at the top. The page jumps or animates too much Open Theme settings \u2192 Motion and choose Calm , or turn Enable scroll animations off. My text is hard to read on an image Change the Text color or Tone of that section, or choose a calmer, darker image. I changed something and want to undo it Press Undo at the top of the editor. Use Actions \u2192 Duplicate to keep a backup before big changes. Can I use apps? Yes. Add app blocks where a section offers Add block \u2192 Apps . Too many apps slow the store, so add only what you need. Can I change the theme code? Please duplicate the theme first . Custom code changes are not covered by support. F"}, {"u": "support.html", "t": "Get support", "g": "Help", "x": "We read every message and reply within two business days.  Before you write Search this guide. Most questions are answered in Troubleshooting . Note the page address where the problem happens. Take a screenshot or a short screen recording. Send a request What support covers Questions about how the theme's settings work Bugs in the theme Custom design changes, adding new features and setting up third-party apps are not covered. A Shopify Partner can help with those. Keep your store safe Never send your password in a request. If we need access, we will ask you to send a collaborator request from your Shopify admin. "}, {"u": "changelog.html", "t": "Changelog", "g": "Help", "x": "What changed in each version.  1.7.1 New Photo shape setting for the product page, featured product, product story and collection banner. Quick buy now has a thumbnail strip with arrows and a counter, like the main product page. Featured product opens on the selected variant's photo. Bundle block can fill itself from Shopify's complementary-product suggestions. Sticky bar has a variant dropdown that stays in sync with the main picker. Product story tabs scroll cleanly on phones. 1.7.0 New colour swatches: clear ring and tick on the chosen swatch, name tooltip, sold-out strike, and automatic text buttons when a colour is missing. New Swatch colors setting to type your own shade colours. Cleaner swatch dots on product cards with a +N count. Documentation rewritten for beginners. 1.6.5 Sample press section now uses fictional publication names. 1.6.4 Added preset listing templates for Lumivane, Nightbloom and Fernmist. Rebuilt the Image banner and Stack cards sections. Switched placeholders to Shopify's built-in placeholder images. Optimised image sizes and loading. "}];